            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "redfish/managers/test_bmc_ipv6.robot",
                    "line": 712,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anusha Dathatri",
                        "email": "anusha.dathatri@gmail.com",
                        "username": "adathatri"
                    },
                    "message": "You should break out of the loop once you find the address that you are looking for.\nAn easier approach is to have a boolean variable with default value false. Set it to true if the given IP is found and break. Based on that value you can take further decisions."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish/managers/test_bmc_ipv6.robot",
                    "line": 712,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Sweta Potthuri",
                        "email": "spotthur@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "swe12345"
                    },
                    "message": "We cannot use break because the patch_list should have the same number of elements as the ipv6_static_defgw_configurations."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish/managers/test_bmc_ipv6.robot",
                    "line": 715,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anusha Dathatri",
                        "email": "anusha.dathatri@gmail.com",
                        "username": "adathatri"
                    },
                    "message": "This will show the test case as passed which is a misnomer as we didnt attempt the test at all. Please use Skip if -- It should show that the test is skipped in the report."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish/managers/test_bmc_ipv6.robot",
                    "line": 715,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Sweta Potthuri",
                        "email": "spotthur@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "swe12345"
                    },
                    "message": "When IP is not found all other keywords are considering it as PASS and using Pass Execution If hence following the same.\nKeywords for reference:\nModify IPv6 Address, Delete IPv6 Address"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish/managers/test_bmc_ipv6.robot",
                    "line": 715,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anusha Dathatri",
                        "email": "anusha.dathatri@gmail.com",
                        "username": "adathatri"
                    },
                    "message": "Your intention is to find the default gateway from the list and try to delete it right?\nIf the default gateway is not found then you are not doing any operation so how does the test pass?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish/managers/test_bmc_ipv6.robot",
                    "line": 715,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Sweta Potthuri",
                        "email": "spotthur@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "swe12345"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, that is the intended behaviour, when there is no default gateway found we are passing the test case.\nWhen the default gateway is found in the addresses then it deletes it else it simply passes the test case with a message that the ipv6 gateway does not exist on the BMC."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish/managers/test_bmc_ipv6.robot",
                    "line": 715,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anusha Dathatri",
                        "email": "anusha.dathatri@gmail.com",
                        "username": "adathatri"
                    },
                    "message": "How will a person know whether the delete operation was successfully performed when they see the test as passed? PASS should indicate that test was able to delete the gateway and verify it. If we didnt even found a valid case to do it then it should say we skipped."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish/managers/test_bmc_ipv6.robot",
                    "line": 715,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Sweta Potthuri",
                        "email": "spotthur@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "swe12345"
                    },
                    "message": "Changing to Skip If"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish/managers/test_bmc_ipv6.robot",
                    "line": 717,
                    "reviewer": {
